  "contract": [
    "One native C release implementation serves public thunk and split stock body. Null/control/range/allocated-bit gates, top coalescing, neighboring free blocks, bin metadata and boundary tags are preserved.",
    "The query retains stock unsigned arithmetic: available minus(top-base+16) only if available exceeds that amount; it is not replaced by a sum of portable free-list nodes.",
    "Bin selection returns0 only for8..1032; insertion uses encoded-header order and circular anchors, removal preserves bitmap clearing. Bin-helper inputs are valid native descriptors with index0 or1."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "484 instruction bytes are accounted across wrappers, split body and helpers;480 execute. The only four unexecuted bytes are0x93e26..0x93e29: the increment path cannot run because guarded(size-8)<=1024 and the first threshold is1024.",
    "4613 release comparisons include all four-block free orders across six size profiles, two alignments, terminal guards and masks, plus explicit invalid pointers.2054 bin comparisons cover low-size domain and high unsigned edges. Null control/query behavior is checked.",
    "500 mixed operations include251 C releases, with stock allocation between them. Complete pool images, descriptor write width/order/value and query results match. Source release is forbidden from entering stock code.",
    "Stock allocation/initialization are used only to prepare fixture data and test interoperability. They do not establish a source-only allocator, reallocator or complete teardown lifecycle.",
    "Saved integer/FP registers, SP, masks, FPSCR and guards are checked. Caller scratch, void return, private frames, APSR, concurrent mutation, malformed list structures, invalid bin indices, physical memory behavior, final startup/scatter integration and boot remain unverified.",
    "No new persistent state. Native provider uses existing r1_goodix_native_heap_pool. Portable model code remains unchanged; only frontier selection is superseded. Source plan/cache layout and import sets remain unchanged."
  ],
